Patches origin
--------------

The ubuntu-tab-x910 kernel deb is the per-device kernel package for SM-X910
(Samsung Galaxy Tab S9 Ultra Wi-Fi). It follows the Mobian per-device
kernel-deb pattern (see https://salsa.debian.org/Mobian-team/devices/kernels/
qcom-linux for the canonical example).

Kernel base
-----------

kernel.org stable/linux at v7.0.6 (linux-7.0.y HEAD); SHA
5d83f95062a860326fd9c69a9d7a1f01063270c1. Tracking branch
upstream-branch = linux-7.0.y (gbp.conf).

Patch sources
-------------

debian/patches/ubuntu-tab-x910/ contains all device- and SoC-layer patches
applied at build time via quilt (debian/source/format = 3.0 (quilt)).

  * 0001-arm64-dts-qcom-add-Samsung-Galaxy-Tab-S9-Ultra-X910.patch
    Leaf DTS for SM-X910 (SKU-keyed filename sm8550-samsung-x910.dts per
    DEC-196). Bootstrap source = Samsung downstream gts9uwifi_eur_open_w00_r03
    .dts SHA 74a08fac2da9984d315616b1e77e00307dfa551d (SoC-plumbing + regulators
    + PCIe-enablement layer; mainline-cleaned). Bucket-B device-DTS off-tree.

  * 0002-arm64-dts-qcom-add-Samsung-Galaxy-Tab-S9-family-common-dtsi.patch
    Factored sm8550-samsung-gts9-common.dtsi for Tab S9 family-shared content
    per DEC-119 + DEC-196 + RFT-116. Bucket-A SoC-layer (intended for upstream
    submission via Konrad Dybcio funnel; see ADR-0027 D4 + R13 ADR-0024 D2).

  * 0003-arm64-configs-add-ubuntu-tab-x910-defconfig.patch
    Per-device defconfig arch/arm64/configs/ubuntu-tab-x910_defconfig.
    Includes the 4 RFT-120 NAMING-FIX corrections (CONFIG_FASTRPC ->
    CONFIG_QCOM_FASTRPC; CONFIG_INPUT_GPIO_KEYS -> CONFIG_KEYBOARD_GPIO;
    CONFIG_QCOM_WDT=m; CONFIG_QCOM_Q6V5_PAS=m) per R13 ADR-0024 D5 + R14
    ADR-0020 D5 + module-signing posture per R15 ADR-0022 D5 + the =m configs
    for fast-cycle module hot-reload per ADR-0027 D9.

Sess-67 milestone-1 build-only scope
-------------------------------------

This is the first build of the ubuntu-tab-x910 kernel deb. Milestone-1 covers
build env + leaf DTS + factored common.dtsi + defconfig + first dpkg-buildpackage
attempt + .deb validation. No boot.img, no Thor flash, no first-boot smoke —
those are milestone-2 (gated on milestone-1 closing cleanly per advisor sess-66
#1; destructive-gate-adjacent per binding-constraint #6).
